    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-10945",
      "problem": "Represent the solution of the inequality $k -12 \\lt  -5$ on a number line.",
      "worked_solution": "To isolate $k,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *subtracting* $12,$ which is *adding* $12.$\nRemember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-12 & <-5 \\\\ k-12+12 & <-5+12 \\\\ k+0 & <7 \\\\ k & <7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k \\lt  7.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192536/assets/9cc25f8eec7586ce65a17be3eb7af6ee509d014bf8dc9896cd45c6ef99769250.png)",
